# Line-ending and binary rules for the LifeTrac repo.
#
# Why: this repo is mostly edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true), but many
# files run on the Portenta X8 boards or inside Linux containers, where a CRLF
# breaks them ("/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter", systemd/udev/mosquitto parse
# errors, `source`d env files with a trailing \r in every value). The rules
# below make Git check those files out with LF on every OS and make
# `git archive` emit LF for them even when core.autocrlf=true.
#
# The index already stores these files with LF, so this file changes checkout
# behaviour only. An EXISTING working tree keeps its old copies until the files
# are checked out again. With a clean tree (commit or set aside your work
# first -- this rewrites every tracked file):
#     git rm --cached -r -q . && git reset --hard
# On a Windows checkout made with core.autocrlf=true that refresh also repairs
# binaries that autocrlf had mangled on checkout (some *.pdf, *.hex, *.zip and
# bench-evidence *.bin files whose content Git guessed was text).
# Board-side deploys should still pass `-c core.autocrlf=false` to
# `git archive`, because files not listed here (.txt, .md, .json, .html, ...)
# follow core.autocrlf.
#
# Files not matched below keep the default behaviour (core.autocrlf).

# --- Runs on the boards / in containers: always LF -------------------------
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
*.socket        text eol=lf
*.rules         text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
*.env           text eol=lf
*.env.example   text eol=lf
requirements*.txt text eol=lf

# --- Windows scripts: CRLF in the working tree ------------------------------
# text=auto leaves anything Git detects as binary (e.g. a UTF-16 file) alone.
*.ps1           text=auto eol=crlf
*.bat           text=auto eol=crlf

# --- Binary: never convert, never text-diff/merge ---------------------------
*.bin           binary
*.elf           binary
*.hex           binary
*.o             binary
*.a             binary
*.exe           binary
*.dll           binary
*.so            binary
*.whl           binary
*.tar           binary
*.tgz           binary
*.gz            binary
*.xz            binary
*.zip           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.png           binary
*.gif           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.rgb           binary
